sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Browser A
  participant Out as External channel
  participant STUN as Google STUN
  participant B as Browser B

  Note over A,B: Manual signaling and ECDH setup
  A->>A: Generate P-256 key pair and WebRTC offer
  A->>STUN: Gather all ICE candidates
  A->>Out: Emoji envelope with offer and public key A
  Out->>B: User transfers envelope
  B->>B: Decode, generate P-256 key pair, derive shared root
  B->>STUN: Gather all ICE candidates
  B->>Out: Emoji envelope with answer and public key B
  Out->>A: User transfers envelope
  A->>A: Decode answer and derive matching shared root
  A->>B: Compare 8-character safety number out of band

  Note over A,B: Direct encrypted conversation
  A->>A: Sort public keys; derive separate A-to-B and B-to-A chains
  B->>B: Sort public keys; derive the same directional chains
  loop Each directional message n
    A->>A: Derive message key and next chain key with HKDF
    A->>A: Pad and encrypt with AES-256-GCM
    A->>B: Send authenticated envelope with sender direction
    B->>B: Derive on temporary ratchet state
    B->>B: Authenticate and decrypt, then commit ratchet state
  end

  alt Data channel closes unexpectedly
    A->>A: Keep send and receive ratchet positions
    A->>A: Pack next encrypted envelope as emoji
    A->>Out: User transfers each fallback message
    Out->>B: User pastes encrypted emoji
    B->>B: Authenticate, decrypt, and continue ratchet
    Note over A,B: Fresh SDP reconnect preserves existing message ratchets
  end
